oose that the Yankees come.","wi":273,"wj":281,"s":168.22,"e":171.14,"corrob":0.8571},{"quote":"I satisfied so far, for the Lord has done for me.","wi":532,"wj":543,"s":261.02,"e":266.06,"corrob":1}]},"chapters":[{"title":"Singing","at":{"quote":"Oh, let me come in. I surrender and open the door.","wi":83,"wj":94,"s":54.56,"e":60.4,"corrob":0.9167}},{"title":"Born in 1844","at":{"quote":"My name is Wallace Quartermann in and through the state of Georgia.","wi":164,"wj":176,"s":101.74,"e":107.16,"corrob":0.9167}},{"title":"The day the big gun shot","at":{"quote":"The overseer asked me what is that of that is thunder.","wi":213,"wj":224,"s":146.32,"e":150.44,"corrob":0.8182}},{"title":"Turn the people loose","at":{"quote":"run down in the field and tell Peter to turn the people loose that the Yankees come.","wi":264,"wj":281,"s":164.58,"e":171.14,"corrob":0.9375}},{"title":"Freedom","at":{"quote":"and give me all freedom, cause we are this much as free as them.","wi":446,"wj":460,"s":228.9,"e":233.98,"corrob":0.7586}}],"concepts":[{"term":"\"Turn the people loose\"","definition":"The order Quarterman carried to the fields as a young man — emancipation not as a proclamation read from a courthouse step, but as a message run from the house to the driver.","cite":{"quote":"turn the people loose that the Yankees come.","wi":273,"wj":281,"s":168.22,"e":171.14,"corrob":0.8571}}],"flags":[]},"notes":[{"id":"loc-quarterman_c1","kind":"quote","text":"The overseer asked me what is that of that is thunder. I tell him I don't know.","quote":"The overseer asked me what is that of that is thunder. I tell him I don't know.","anchor":{"s":146.32,"e":152.52,"wi":213,"wj":230,"quality":"word"},"heard":false,"createdAt":1787443200000,"updatedAt":1787443200000},{"id":"loc-quarterman_c0","kind":"point","text":"He was about 21 when freedom came — old enough to be the one who carried the message.","quote":"turn the people loose that the Yankees come.","anchor":{"s":168.22,"e":171.14,"wi":273